%% Core session loop: the engineer's build-deploy-watch-homecoming cycle (r2, positive valence).
%% Granularity is "what screen am I on and what did I just do", not micro-interactions.
flowchart TD
    Workshop["Workshop\nkitbash the mech tree, equip pilot skills (gated by parts),\ntune the pilot-machine fit, read the sync forecast"]
    Gamble{"Deploy gamble\n(fit readout: how she handles this frame)"}
    Detune["Detune / fit her better\nsafe, steady growth this run"]
    Theatre["Theatre\nread the living war, pick a front to deploy to"]
    Deploy["Deploy\nhand the friend + machine to the war\n(point of no control)"]
    Watch["Watch the duel\nsync climbs toward a breakthrough,\nyour mech vs an enemy mech, war shifting around it"]
    Outcome{"Battle result"}
    HomeWin["Homecoming — win\nXP toward skills, higher sync ceiling, salvage;\nbreakthrough if you pushed a stretch fit"]
    HomeLoss["Homecoming — survived loss\nless XP/salvage, a harder road next;\nno harm to the pilot"]

    Workshop --> Gamble
    Gamble -->|"detune / improve fit"| Detune
    Detune --> Workshop
    Gamble -->|"push as-is for the breakthrough"| Theatre
    Theatre --> Deploy
    Deploy --> Watch
    Watch --> Outcome
    Outcome -->|"won"| HomeWin
    Outcome -->|"lost but survives"| HomeLoss
    HomeWin --> Workshop
    HomeLoss --> Workshop
